# The index of the absolute weak normalization diagram is filtered

For a commutative ring `A`, `Algebra.AbsoluteWeakNormalizationIndex A` is a small model of the
category of finitely presented `A`-algebras whose structure morphism on spectra is a universal
homeomorphism.  This file proves that this category is filtered, which is the hypothesis under
which the filtered-colimit theorem
`AlgebraicGeometry.universalHomeomorphism_specMap_of_isColimit` applies to
`Algebra.absoluteWeakNormalizationDiagram A`, and deduces that the canonical morphism
`Spec (Aᵃʷⁿ) ⟶ Spec A` is a universal homeomorphism.

## Main results

* The filtered structure of the index category is
  `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_cocone_objs_absoluteWeakNormalization` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.exists_cocone_maps_absoluteWeakNormalization` of
  `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Topologies/WeakNormalization/RingColimitFiltered.lean`, which
  this module imports and does not restate.

## Implementation notes

This is the absolute weak normalization counterpart of
`StacksDraft.AlgebraicGeometry.F3.Seminormalization.IndexFiltered`, and the two arguments for
filteredness are the same two: the tensor product `B ⊗[A] C` is finitely presented and again a
universal homeomorphism over `A` by base change, and two parallel maps `f, g : B ⟶ C` are
equalized by `C ⧸ I` for `I` generated by the finitely many differences `f bᵢ - g bᵢ` over a
finite generating set of `B`.  Every element of `I` is nilpotent, which is where the geometry
enters; that input is
`AlgebraicGeometry.isNilpotent_sub_of_universalHomeomorphism`, which is consumed from the
seminormalization development rather than restated, since it does not mention residue fields.

Two differences from the seminormalization case make this the shorter argument.  The objects of
`Algebra.absoluteWeakNormalizationObject A` are honest `A`-algebras rather than explicit finite
presentations, so no step transporting a construction back onto a representative is needed; and
there is no condition on residue fields, so only the universal-homeomorphism half of each step
is required.  Filteredness is proved for the full subcategory cut out by the object property and
then transported to `Algebra.AbsoluteWeakNormalizationIndex A`, which is its small model, along
`CategoryTheory.equivSmallModel`.

Everything lives in a single universe `u`, as `AlgebraicGeometry.UniversalHomeomorphism` is
available only for `Scheme.{u}`.

No hypothesis beyond those of Tag 0EUR is used: `A` is an arbitrary commutative ring, with no
Noetherian or reducedness assumption.

## What is not done

Nothing here says that `Algebra.AbsoluteWeakNormalization A` is *terminal* among `A`-algebras
whose spectrum morphism is a universal homeomorphism, and nothing here constructs a map into or
out of it.  That statement needs, in addition, the presentation of an arbitrary such algebra as
a filtered colimit of finitely presented ones (Tag 0EUJ), for which no declaration exists in the
Lean libraries of this repository.  Consequently the characterization of when the canonical map
to the absolute weak normalization is an isomorphism (Tag 0EUR), and with it the initiality of
`AlgebraicGeometry.UniversalHomeomorphismOver X` and the characterization of when its map to
another universal homeomorphism is an isomorphism (both Tag 0EUS), are still unproved after this
file.

No `@[stacks]` tag is attached here.  Tag 0EUR's three live labels are the two ring colimits
themselves, which are already formalized in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Morphisms.WeakNormalization.RingColimit`; the properties of those
colimits proved here are, in the source, part of the proof of the remaining 0EUR labels
`awn_final` and `awn_characterization`, neither of which is complete.

